ut 2,200 years old; it is also said to date from the 14th century. Some years ago, when Panyas Pravar Shri Rajendravijayji visited Dholka, he was struck with wonder the moment he saw this beautiful image. He wished to install this ancient image in a temple. A grand temple was accordingly built, and this image was installed by the venerable hands of Acharya Kanaksurishwarji on the third day of the bright half of the month of Falgun, V.S. 2038. On this occasion, Panyas Pravar Shri Rajendravijayji was honoured with the title of Acharya.. This temple also contains very ancient and striking images of Lord Adinath and Lord Shitalnath. In front of it stands the eye-catching Dadawadi of the great Kharatargachchha acharya Shri Jindattasurishwarji. About 85 years ago, when the foundation was being laid for a separate temple, excavation in the courtyard uncovered 34 ancient images, which are still kept in the Lord Adinath temple. On this ground, behind the Kalikund Parshwanath temple, a model \\\"Mini-Shatrunjay\\\" tirtha has been built as a replica of the sacred Shatrunjay pilgrimage site.. Other Temples: There are 3 other ancient temples here. In the temple of Lord Sumatinath, the image of Lord Neminath is charming. There is also an ancient temple of Lord Adinath here, where this ancient image of Lord Parshwanath was found; the Adinath image is believed to date from the time of King Samprati. In front of this temple stands a Dadawadi.. Art and Sculpture: This ancient image displays exquisite artistry — the Lord appears to bless devotees with steady eyes and a lovely smile. The temple's architecture is entirely distinctive, and the hoods of this Parshwanath image differ completely from those of other images.. Directions: The nearest railway station to the temple, Dholka, is 1 km away. The temple stands on the Vadodara–Palitana road. Ahmedabad is 40 km, Palitana 190 km, and Vallabhipur 110 km away. Regular bus services to Ahmedabad are available. Dharamshala and bhojanshala facilities are available. The pilgrimage sites of Matar, Kheda, Khambhat, and Sojitra are nearby. Dholka is one of the shrines of the Matru Panchtirthi (the five \\\"mother\\\" shrines).. Scripture References: Kalikund Parshwanath is mentioned in \\\"Tirthvandana,\\\" the \\\"Shri Parshwanath\\\" biography, \\\"Shri Prabhakar Charitra,\\\" \\\"Shri Abhaydev Charitra,\\\" \\\"Tirthmala,\\\" \\\"Guruvali,\\\" \\\"365 Shri Parshwajin Nammala,\\\" \\\"Shri Shankheshwar Parshwanath Chhand,\\\" \\\"Shri Bhatewa Parshwanath Stavan,\\\" \\\"108 Namgarbhit Shri Bhagwan Parshwanath Stavan,\\\" \\\"Shri Parshwanath Sankhya Stavan,\\\" \\\"Shri Parshwanath Nammala,\\\" \\\"135 Namgarbhit Shri Parshwanath Stavan,\\\" \\\"Shri Subhadra Sati Ras,\\\" \\\"Shri Parshwa Prabhu ke 108 Naam ke Chhand,\\\" and others.. Temples of Kalikund Parshwanath: At Dandherwada (Patan), Kankan Parshwanath is also known as Kalikund Parshwanath, or Vinchhiya Parshwanath. Images are also found at the Gagan Vihar flats in Ahmedabad, at Kapadvanj, at Calicut in Kerala, at Ajhadgali in Kolhapur, at Kumbhajgiri (Dharamshala Theli), at Santacruz in Mumbai, near Desai Pol Pedhi in Surat, at Jaisalmer, and at Bharuch. On the sacred hills of Shatrunjay, where two paths meet, stands a deri (small shrine) of Kalikund Parshwanath. Images of Kalikund Parshwanath are also found at Bhildiyaji Tirtha, Jiravala Tirtha, Chandanbala Apartments in Mumbai, the Shri Adinath Temple at Walkeshwar in Mumbai, and Hathibhai ni Wadi in Ahmedabad.. Hymn of Praise: Taking initiation, he came to dwell in the Vanakhand forest; on the bank of a pond he stood absorbed in kayotsarga meditation; there, by means of an elephant bearing a lotus, worship was offered to Lord Parshwa — \\\"With loving devotion I bow in reverence to Shri Kalikund Parshwa...\\\". Chanting Mantra: \\\"Om Hreem Arham Shri Kalikund Parshwanathaya Namah\\\". Trust: Shri Kalikund Parshwanath Jain Shwetambar Tirth, c/o Shri Tejpal Vastu Jain Dharmagranth Trust, Post: Dholka – 387810, District: Ahmedabad, State: Gujarat, India. Phone: 02714-225218, 02714-225738, Mobile: 9427030982.. History of the 108 Parshwanath Dadas and how to reach them... Part 6: After completing pilgrimage to a total of 16 Parshwanath Lord shrines — 4 at Navsari, Surat and Rader; 2 at Bharuch and Gandhar; 4 at Dabhoi, Chhani and Borsad; 4 at Khambhat; and 2 at Kheda and Dholka — we will next travel to the 4 Parshwanath Lord shrines of Ahmedabad. Dholka to Ahmedabad – 40 km.. Ahmedabad: 17. Shri Shamla Parshwanath, 18. Shri Muleva Parshwanath, 19. Shri Hrikar Parshwanath, 20. Shri Sukhsagar Parshwanath.. In Ahmedabad, the Jin Aagna Yuva Group arranges auto-rickshaws for pilgrims visiting the city's shrines (number 09558845672). This group gives preference to calling Jain auto-rickshaw drivers first.. Bhojanshala and Dharamshala in Ahmedabad: 1. Seth Dalpatbhai Bhagubhai Marchipol Jain Dharamshala, Marchipol, Ratanpol, Ahmedabad, Phone – 079-25359624. 2. Hathisingh ni Dharamshala, Shahibaug, Bardolpur, Delhi Darwaza, Ahmedabad, Phone – 079-22180774.. Hymn in Praise of Lord Parshwanath:. O Lord of kings, Lord of serpent-lords, Lord of gods, sovereign over hundreds of Indras — I worship you and bow my head before you; great sages and heads of monastic orders bow to you with joined hands — salutations forever to the god of gods, Parshwanath. (1). You free those seized by mighty elephants and lions, you save from great calamity and danger; you grant victory in the fiercest of battles, and free devotees from severe disease and bondage. (2). 17. Shri Shamla Parshwanath – Shamlajini Pol, Shamlaji no Khancho, Madangopal ni Haveli, Ahmedabad – 380001.. Main Deity: An image of Lord Shri Shamla Parshwanath in black stone, about 35 centimetres tall, in the padmasana posture, with a canopy of 7 serpent hoods above the head.. Location: This is in Shyamalji ni Pol in the city of Ahmedabad.. History: This is an ancient temple dating to the 17th century, built in V.S. 1656 by Sanghvi Somji and his brother Shiv, descendants of minister Vastupal.. Art and Sculpture: The wood carvings here beautifully depict scenes from the auspicious celebrations (kalyanak mahotsav) of the Tirthankaras. This temple is famous for its extraordinary wood carving, without parallel. The marble image of Lord Parshwanath in the kayotsarga posture is very striking and beautiful. This image of Shamla Parshwanath is ancient, attractive, and impressive.. Other Temples: Ahmedabad has more than 400 temples, and many, being ancient, are regarded as pilgrimage sites.. Directions: Ahmedabad is a very famous city of Gujarat, well connected by rail, road, and air to all the cities of India. There are more than 100 upashrayas, and several dharamshalas and bhojanshalas. There are many jnanabhandars where ancient books are preserved. Many handwritten manuscripts are preserved in the upashraya of Doshiwad Pol and other places in Ahmedabad.. Scripture References: Shri Shamla Parshwanath is mentioned in \\\"365 Shri Parshwanath Nammala,\\\" \\\"Shri Shankheshwar Parshwanath Chhand,\\\" \\\"Shri Bhatewa Parshwanath Stavan,\\\" \\\"Garbhagriha Shri Parshwanath Stavan,\\\" \\\"Patan Chaitya Paripati,\\\" \\\"Tirthmala,\\\" and others.. There are several temples of Shyamla Parshwanath in India — the main temple is in Ahmedabad at Shyamalji ni Pol; in addition there are Shyamla Parshwanath temples at Devsano Pado and at Hailamesar ni Pol.\"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,\"1b:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"div\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"mb-8 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"a\\\",null,{\\\"href\\\":\\\"https://goo.gl/maps/xrgPwPYiUY2BzWSv5\\\",\\\"target\\\":\\\"_blank\\\",\\\"rel\\\":\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\",\\\"className\\\":\\\"inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-sm bg-maroon px-5 py-2.5 font-ui text-sm font-medium text-ivory hover:bg-maroon-deep transition-colors\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"$L1a\\\",null,{\\\"ref\\\":\\\"$undefi