h (Dholka) and Shri Shamla Parshwanath (Ahmedabad) फोटो 3\\\",\\\"fill\\\":true,\\\"sizes\\\":\\\"(min-width: 640px) 33vw, 50vw\\\",\\\"className\\\":\\\"object-cover\\\"}]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"div\\\",\\\"9317d465-d2ed-43d2-bccd-bbbcd08b06a7\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"relative overflow-hidden rounded-sm bg-sandstone-deep/30 aspect-square\\\",\\\"children\\\":[\\\"$\\\",\\\"$L22\\\",null,{\\\"src\\\":\\\"https://iiudzezqkqtqcxbkssdq.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/tirtha-images/img_7440.jpeg\\\",\\\"alt\\\":\\\"Shri Kalikund Parshwanath (Dholka) and Shri Shamla Parshwanath (Ahmedabad) फोटो 4\\\",\\\"fill\\\":true,\\\"sizes\\\":\\\"(min-width: 640px) 33vw, 50vw\\\",\\\"className\\\":\\\"object-cover\\\"}]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"div\\\",\\\"f6cf53d3-70f6-4f3f-88bd-c8d091b80f38\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"relative overflow-hidden rounded-sm bg-sandstone-deep/30 aspect-square\\\",\\\"children\\\":[\\\"$\\\",\\\"$L22\\\",null,{\\\"src\\\":\\\"https://iiudzezqkqtqcxbkssdq.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/tirtha-images/img_7446.jpeg\\\",\\\"alt\\\":\\\"Shri Kalikund Parshwanath (Dholka) and Shri Shamla Parshwanath (Ahmedabad) फोटो 5\\\",\\\"fill\\\":true,\\\"sizes\\\":\\\"(min-width: 640px) 33vw, 50vw\\\",\\\"className\\\":\\\"object-cover\\\"}]}]]}]\\n\"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,\"1d:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"article\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"prose-none space-y-4 font-body text-[1.05rem] leading-[1.85] text-ink\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"0\\\",{\\\"children\\\":\\\"(Continued) ...was appointed as [governor]. During this period Jain dharma flourished greatly, and much Jain literature was composed here at that time.\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"1\\\",{\\\"children\\\":\\\"Minister Vastupal built here a beautiful temple of Lord Adinath and 2 upashrayas. In the 14th century, minister Pethashah of Mandavgadh built a temple here which no longer stands. Even today there are 3 ancient temples here. In the basement (tahkhana) of the Lord's temple is a striking image of Adinath and of Lord Kalikund Parshwanath, believed to be about 2,200 years old; it is also said to date from the 14th century. Some years ago, when Panyas Pravar Shri Rajendravijayji visited Dholka, he was struck with wonder the moment he saw this beautiful image. He wished to install this ancient image in a temple. A grand temple was accordingly built, and this image was installed by the venerable hands of Acharya Kanaksurishwarji on the third day of the bright half of the month of Falgun, V.S. 2038. On this occasion, Panyas Pravar Shri Rajendravijayji was honoured with the title of Acharya.\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"2\\\",{\\\"children\\\":\\\"This temple also contains very ancient and striking images of Lord Adinath and Lord Shitalnath. In front of it stands the eye-catching Dadawadi of the great Kharatargachchha acharya Shri Jindattasurishwarji. About 85 years ago, when the foundation was being laid for a separate temple, excavation in the courtyard uncovered 34 ancient images, which are still kept in the Lord Adinath temple. On this ground, behind the Kalikund Parshwanath temple, a model \\\\\\\"Mini-Shatrunjay\\\\\\\" tirtha has been built as a replica of the sacred Shatrunjay pilgrimage site.\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"3\\\",{\\\"children\\\":\\\"Other Temples: There are 3 other ancient temples here. In the temple of Lord Sumatinath, the image of Lord Neminath is charming. There is also an ancient temple of Lord Adinath here, where this ancient image of Lord Parshwanath was found; the Adinath image is believed to date from the time of King Samprati. In front of this temple stands a Dadawadi.\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"4\\\",{\\\"children\\\":\\\"Art and Sculpture: This ancient image displays exquisite artistry — the Lord appears to bless devotees with steady eyes and a lovely smile. The temple's architecture is entirely distinctive, and the hoods of this Parshwanath image differ completely from those of other images.\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"5\\\",{\\\"children\\\":\\\"Directions: The nearest railway station to the temple, Dholka, is 1 km away. The temple stands on the Vadodara–Palitana road. Ahmedabad is 40 km, Palitana 190 km, and Vallabhipur 110 km away. Regular bus services to Ahmedabad are available. Dharamshala and bhojanshala facilities are available. The pilgrimage sites of Matar, Kheda, Khambhat, and Sojitra are nearby. Dholka is one of the shrines of the Matru Panchtirthi (the five \\\\\\\"mother\\\\\\\" shrines).\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"6\\\",{\\\"children\\\":\\\"Scripture References: Kalikund Parshwanath is mentioned in \\\\\\\"Tirthvandana,\\\\\\\" the \\\\\\\"Shri Parshwanath\\\\\\\" biography, \\\\\\\"Shri Prabhakar Charitra,\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"Shri Abhaydev Charitra,\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"Tirthmala,\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"Guruvali,\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"365 Shri Parshwajin Nammala,\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"Shri Shankheshwar Parshwanath Chhand,\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"Shri Bhatewa Parshwanath Stavan,\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"108 Namgarbhit Shri Bhagwan Parshwanath Stavan,\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"Shri Parshwanath Sankhya Stavan,\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"Shri Parshwanath Nammala,\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"135 Namgarbhit Shri Parshwanath Stavan,\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"Shri Subhadra Sati Ras,\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"Shri Parshwa Prabhu ke 108 Naam ke Chhand,\\\\\\\" and others.\\\"}],\\\"$L23\\\",\\\"$L24\\\",\\\"$L25\\\",\\\"$L26\\\",\\\"$L27\\\",\\\"$L28\\\",\\\"$L29\\\",\\\"$L2a\\\",\\\"$L2b\\\",\\\"$L2c\\\",\\\"$L2d\\\",\\\"$L2e\\\",\\\"$L2f\\\",\\\"$L30\\\",\\\"$L31\\\",\\\"$L32\\\",\\\"$L33\\\",\\\"$L34\\\",\\\"$L35\\\",\\\"$L36\\\"]}]\\n\"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,\"1e:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"nav\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"mt-14 flex items-center justify-between border-t border-sandstone-deep/60 pt-6\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"$L5\\\",null,{\\\"href\\\":\\\"/en/tirtha/tirtha-018\\\",\\\"className\\\":\\\"group flex items-center gap-1.5 font-ui text-sm text-ink-soft hover:text-maroon transition-colors\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\