carvings here beautifully depict scenes from the auspicious celebrations (kalyanak mahotsav) of the Tirthankaras. This temple is famous for its extraordinary wood carving, without parallel. The marble image of Lord Parshwanath in the kayotsarga posture is very striking and beautiful\"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,\". This image of Shamla Parshwanath is ancient, attractive, and impressive.\\\"}]\\n33:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"23\\\",{\\\"children\\\":\\\"Other Temples: Ahmedabad has more than 400 temples, and many, being ancient, are regarded as pilgrimage sites.\\\"}]\\n34:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"24\\\",{\\\"children\\\":\\\"Directions: Ahmedabad is a very famous city of Gujarat, well connected by rail, road, and air to all the cities of India. There are more than 100 upashrayas, and several dharamshalas and bhojanshalas. There are many jnanabhandars where ancient books are preserved. Many handwritten manuscripts are preserved in the upashraya of Doshiwad Pol and other places in Ahmedabad.\\\"}]\\n35:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"25\\\",{\\\"children\\\":\\\"Scripture References: Shri Shamla Parshwanath is mentioned in \\\\\\\"365 Shri Parshwanath Nammala,\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"Shri Shankheshwar Parshwanath Chhand,\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"Shri Bhatewa Parshwanath Stavan,\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"Garbhagriha Shri Parshwanath Stavan,\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"Patan Chaitya Paripati,\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"Tirthmala,\\\\\\\" and others.\\\"}]\\n36:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"26\\\",{\\\"children\\\":\\\"There are several temples of Shyamla Parshwanath in India — the main temple is in Ahmedabad at Shyamalji ni Pol; in addition there are Shyamla Parshwanath temples at Devsano Pado and at Hailamesar ni Pol.\\\"}]\\n\"])</script></body></html>","rscData":"","segmentData":{"/_tree":"","/_full":"","/$d$lang/tirtha/$d$slug/__PAGE__":"","/$d$lang/tirtha/$d$slug":"","/$d$lang/tirtha":"","/$d$lang":"","/_index":"","/_head":""},"headers":{"x-nextjs-stale-time":"300","x-nextjs-prerender":"1","x-next-cache-tags":"_N_T